</section>
<section class="review-section" id="faq">
<h2><svg class="neon-icon" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3"></path><line x1="12" x2="12.01" y1="17" y2="17"></line></svg> Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Can I use Maket AI for commercial projects?</div><div class="faq-answer">Yes, Professional and Studio plans include full commercial licensing. You can use AI-generated floor plans in client projects, for sale, or in real estate development without additional fees.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">How accurate are the floor plans?</div><div class="faq-answer">Maket AI generates dimensionally accurate floor plans suitable for concept presentations and preliminary design. However, they should be reviewed and refined by a licensed architect before construction.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Can I import my own site plans?</div><div class="faq-answer">Currently, you input lot dimensions manually. Direct import of CAD or PDF site plans is not yet supported but is on the roadmap for future releases.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Does Maket AI work for commercial buildings?</div><div class="faq-answer">No, Maket AI is specifically optimized for residential architecture. For commercial projects, consider alternatives like Hypar or TestFit.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Can I edit the generated floor plans?</div><div class="faq-answer">You can regenerate with different parameters and choose from variations, but in-app editing is limited. Most users export to CAD or BIM software for detailed modifications.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">What file formats can I export?</div><div class="faq-answer">Currently, high-quality PDF is the primary export format. DWG and Revit export are planned features. The PDFs include dimensions and can be imported into most CAD software.</div></div>
</section>
